      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Have you ever touched a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "sensitive plant",
            "zh": "含羞草"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "? If you do, its leaves will close. How "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "interesting",
            "ref": "v-interesting"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The sensitive plant is also called “touch-me-not”. It grows in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Central and South America",
            "zh": "中南美洲"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Some people keep it as a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "houseplant",
            "zh": "室内植物"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They think its "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "reaction",
            "ref": "v-reaction"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to touch is fun."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "But why is the sensitive plant so shy? When you touch the leaves of a sensitive plant, the water in its leaves and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "stalks",
            "zh": "茎"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " runs to its "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "base",
            "zh": "底部，根基"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Then, the leaves close and the stalks "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "droop",
            "zh": "垂落"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". This makes the plant look "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "wilted",
            "zh": "枯萎的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Many animals and insects eat plants. The sensitive plant learnt to wilt quickly to "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "scare them away",
            "ref": "v-scare-away"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It doesn’t look tasty when it’s wilted, so plant eaters will go and find another plant for dinner."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "If you touch a sensitive plant and it wilts, don’t be afraid! It’s still a healthy plant. It will send water back to its leaves and stand up "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "straight",
            "ref": "v-straight"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " again."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
